# ElTo kernel - trim fragment (stability).
# Target: QEMU/KVM VMs and ordinary desktop/laptop hardware. What is removed is
# hardware and subsystems outside that target. Every line is "# CONFIG_X is not set";
# merge_config.sh applies it after the CachyOS config and config-elto.fragment.
# Rationale per group is in each comment. Revert any line if real hardware needs it.

# Other hypervisors: ElTo runs on bare metal or QEMU/KVM only.
# CONFIG_XEN is not set
# CONFIG_HYPERV is not set
# CONFIG_VMWARE_PVSCSI is not set
# CONFIG_VMWARE_BALLOON is not set
# CONFIG_VMWARE_VMCI is not set
# CONFIG_VMWARE_VMCI_VSOCKETS is not set
# CONFIG_HYPERV_VSOCKETS is not set

# SAN / enterprise storage: no Fibre Channel, SAS HBAs, iSCSI offload, NVMe fabrics or target mode, NVDIMM/CXL persistent memory.
# CONFIG_INFINIBAND is not set
# CONFIG_NVME_FABRICS is not set
# CONFIG_NVME_RDMA is not set
# CONFIG_NVME_FC is not set
# CONFIG_NVME_TCP is not set
# CONFIG_NVME_TARGET is not set
# CONFIG_SCSI_FC_ATTRS is not set
# CONFIG_SCSI_SAS_ATTRS is not set
# CONFIG_SCSI_SAS_LIBSAS is not set
# CONFIG_SCSI_SPI_ATTRS is not set
# CONFIG_MEGARAID_MM is not set
# CONFIG_MEGARAID_MAILBOX is not set
# CONFIG_MEGARAID_LEGACY is not set
# CONFIG_MEGARAID_SAS is not set
# CONFIG_SCSI_MPT2SAS is not set
# CONFIG_SCSI_MPT3SAS is not set
